# NOTICE: data sources, licensing, attribution

The persian skill bundles small, hand-curated seed data and is designed to scale by ingesting the
open-source banks below into `scripts/data/*.tsv` (format: EN <TAB> FA <TAB> note).

## Currently bundled (seed, hand-curated)
- `scripts/data/idioms.tsv`, `scripts/data/glossary.tsv`: term/idiom pairs authored for this
  skill. No third-party text is redistributed.

## Approved for bundling (ingest to scale): verify each license at ingest time
- **PersianIdioms / Idiom_Translation** (Rezaeimanesh et al., NAACL 2025): ~2,200 FA idioms
  with meanings + EN↔FA idiom sentence pairs. Source for `idioms.tsv`.
  https://github.com/sara-rezaeimanesh/idiom_translation · https://aclanthology.org/2025.naacl-long.405/
- **English-Persian Word Database**: large EN→FA word list, DB-ready. Source for `glossary.tsv`.
  https://github.com/semnan-university-ai/English-Persian-Word-Database
- **EnglishToPersianDictionaries**: aggregated EN→FA dictionaries.
  https://github.com/VahidN/EnglishToPersianDictionaries
- **Wiktionary (via kaikki.org)**: EN headwords with FA glosses + idioms. **License: CC-BY-SA.**
  If ingested, the skill must (a) attribute Wiktionary/kaikki and (b) share-alike any
  redistributed derivative. Tag CC-BY-SA-derived rows so the obligation stays traceable.

## Reference only: DO NOT bundle (consult/cite at runtime)
- **FarsNet** (Persian WordNet, SBU): request/license.
- **Hayyim New Persian–English Dictionary** (DSAL / U. Chicago): online.
- **Aryanpour / Abadis (آبادیس)**: online lookup.
- **LIDIOMS**: multilingual linked idioms (academic).
- **ELRA English–Persian idioms DB**: licensed/paid.
